 "description": "Scratch audit kit for the waterfall/rapids/mist audit (docs/research/rendering/waterfall-assets-vault-audit.md). Vanilla Skyrim FX sheets, skirts, mist blasts and rapids planes, converted to check what survives NIF->glTF: geometry, UVs, texture resolution and alpha. Every entry sets doubleSided because these FX planes are two-sided in the NIF (BSEffectShaderProperty shader flag 2 bit 0x10) and the kit builder otherwise infers sidedness from the asset category, which only knows about foliage. The UV-scroll controllers that animate these in-engine do NOT survive the export; their rates are recorded in the audit doc so our own shader can reproduce them. Not a runtime kit.",
